      "side": 1,
      "message": "Now that nodes live in the shared NetconfTopologyImpl, who removes them when the call-home servers stop? AbstractCallHomeSessionContextManager.close() closes the contexts without calling the overridden remove(id), so disableCallHomeNode() only runs if the SSH sessionClosed event happens to find the context first. Could the two context managers override close() to disable their nodes, like LegacyCallHomeTopology does with deleteAllNodes()?",
